@prefix triage: <urn:atm:triage:> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:atm:triage:finding/AG20-BLOCK-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AG20-BLOCK-003" ;
  triage:title "Transport-owned replay -- persistence extracted but ownership not moved" ;
  triage:description "PeerClientTransport::replay_store (crates/atm-daemon/src/peer_transport/mod.rs:152-171 across sprints) still owns replay persistence from inside the transport module tree despite AG.20's sprint doc explicitly naming replay_store for deletion/relocation out of the transport layer. persist_replay_request function is marked dead_code with explicit reasons ('retained for legacy replay-persistence contract tests while the explicit-endpoint path is used in production dispatch' on s21) — direct admission that production code path has shifted but old API remains as dead code in production. This is a boundary violation: even dead code in the transport module tree violates the AG.20+ scope to remove replay_store ownership entirely from the transport layer. The issue persists through all eight active sprints (s18-s25) as of latest TriageMode=followup_pass sweep." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "blocking" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-19T10:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG20-BLOCK-003/s18/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG20-BLOCK-003/s19/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG20-BLOCK-003/s20/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG20-BLOCK-003/s21/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG20-BLOCK-003/s21/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG20-BLOCK-003/s22/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG20-BLOCK-003/s23/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG20-BLOCK-003/s24/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AG20-BLOCK-003/s25/1> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s18/e46c3a6d> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s19/5d20ca5a> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s20/50572166> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s21/758732cd> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s22/c9aedbcc> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s23/a13fc219> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s24/81298e32> ;
  triage:openOn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s25/c245c2ea> ;
  triage:promoteTo <urn:atm:triage:worktree/s25/c245c2ea> ;
  triage:notes "Followup_pass confirms issue STILL OPEN through all sprints. Replay_store struct field persists on peer_transport/mod.rs lines 152-171 (line numbers shift slightly across sprints due to minor refactors). Dead_code annotations on persist_replay_request acknowledge production code path has shifted to persist_replay_request_to_endpoint (explicit-endpoint version), but legacy function retained for tests and remains in production codebase tree. Boundary violation: dead code in transport module tree = violation of transport-layer scope boundary. highest_open_branch = feature/pAG-s25-live-two-daemon-proof (c245c2ea). All sprints still open; promote_to = s25 (latest active branch). Fix targets s25; merge-forward closes lower branches." .

